# Walkthrough Engine — compiled in-app walkthroughs for the schools/admin surface
# Last updated: 2026-08-08 (move-a-teacher-between-classes joins the class-detail set;
#               2026-08-06 co-teaching coverage: share-a-class, invite-a-supply-teacher,
#               hand-over-the-lead; card genre extracted to WalkCard.vue, shared with the
#               org onboarding gate — one teaching voice, two mounts; the password and
#               install actions get a permanent home and become real pack walks)
# Spec source: docs/walkthrough-engine-scout.md (founder-ratified build spec)

vision: >
  User-visible documentation is dead. Every schools/admin verb that earns one
  gets a guided in-app walkthrough — the PWA install walker's genre (learner-
  paced Next/Back, step dots, pulse-ring pointer) anchored to REAL elements by
  reference. Walkthroughs are COMPILED artifacts: hand-authored JSON, drift-
  gated against the live Vue source so a renamed button FAILS THE BUILD, not
  the user. Zero runtime LLM calls.

architecture:
  authoring:
    tools/walkthrough/walks/*.json: hand-authored walks (the DECISIONS)
    schema: id, title, personas[], place{route,kinds?}, steps[{anchor, say, advance{on}, terminal?}]
    advance_kinds:
      next: explicit tap on the overlay's Next (default — pure show-and-point)
      click: the anchored element's OWN click advances (overlay listens capture-phase, never intercepts, never performs)
      visible: step waits for its anchor to appear, then auto-advances
  compiler:
    tools/walkthrough/lib.mjs: pure gates (unit-tested via player-vue vitest)
    tools/walkthrough/compile.mjs: CLI — `--check` validates, default writes pack
    gates:
      - anchor existence: every step anchor must exist as data-walk="<id>" in packages/player-vue/src/**/*.vue (missing = FAIL; orphan = warning)
      - persona visibility: a walk offered to member personas (leader/school_admin/teacher) must not anchor to an element behind v-if="!member" (FAIL)
      - place validity: place.route must be in useWalkthrough.ts KNOWN_PLACES (lockstep, FAIL)
      - offer lockstep: every walk:<id> CTA in tools/explainer/rules.json must name a pack walk; evaluateRules.ts must handle the 'walk:' prefix (FAIL)
      - safety denylist: click-advance steps must never anchor destructive/minting verbs (delete/purge/entitlement/rotate/revoke/submit/grant/expire/play/toggle) (FAIL)
      - never-auto-play (structural): startWalk() in .vue sources may only appear inside an @click handler — a mounted-hook/watcher/query-param autostart FAILS the build
      - runtime-denylist lockstep: useWalkthrough.ts must mirror DESTRUCTIVE_ANCHOR_PATTERNS verbatim (the stale-pack defence below) — drift FAILS the build
    ci_wiring: src/walkthrough/compileGate.test.ts runs the CLI --check inside `pnpm --filter player-vue test` — the existing CI gates carry it
  pack:
    packages/player-vue/src/walkthrough/pack.json: compiled, bundled static (version = content hash)
    docs/walkthrough-pack.md: human render, DO NOT EDIT
  runtime:
    packages/player-vue/src/walkthrough/useWalkthrough.ts: module-singleton state machine (startWalk/stopWalk/next/back, walksFor persona×place×kind); stamps <html data-walk-active="id:step[:done]"> for e2e assertion; Esc keydown ends the walk (engine-level escape hatch, bound on start/unbound on stop); effectiveAdvance() degrades click-advance on a destructive anchor to show-and-point (runtime mirror of the compiler denylist — a stale/hand-edited pack cannot click-advance a destructive verb)
    packages/player-vue/src/walkthrough/overlayPlacement.ts: pure geometry — placeCard() never places the card into the top-chrome zone (54px + measured safe-area-inset-top: the Learn escape / back-to-player one-tap invariant), bottom-center placement clears safe-area-inset-bottom; isAnchorUsable() rejects zero-size (hidden) elements
    packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/WalkCard.vue: the CARD GENRE on its own — kicker, markdown-lite say, step dots, paced Back/Next, optional × skip, plus a slot for whatever the step needs done. Purely presentational: no state, no flow, no knowledge of the pack. Extracted 2026-08-06 so the org lane's ManagerOnboardingGate can teach in exactly this voice without a second implementation. `dismissible: false` is the rare deliberate case (the org password step has no skip).
    packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/WalkOverlay.vue: the ONE overlay, mounted once in App.vue (async). Pulse-ring on the anchor rect, card with dots/Back/Next/Skip, unanchored fallback after 5s (never hangs) with a slow re-poll so a late anchor re-binds, hidden/zero-size anchors treated as unresolved, pointer-events none except the card (never a modal trap), walk ends on route change
    packages/player-vue/src/components/admin/WalkOffer.vue: quiet "Show me — <title>" text links per persona×place

playback_guardrails:  # runtime rails, each unit-tested (2026-07-28 guardrails pass)
  never_auto_play: engine has no autostart path; compile gate makes it structural (startWalk only inside @click)
  safe_verbs_on_real_data: build-time denylist (gate) + runtime mirror (effectiveAdvance) — defence in depth against a stale pack
  anchor_drift_at_runtime: bounded 5s wait -> unanchored-with-Next; zero-size anchors never bind (no ring at 0,0); re-poll continues after timeout; retrack re-resolves on unmount OR collapse
  escape_hatches: Skip button on every step + Esc key (engine-level) + route change ends the walk; page under the overlay stays fully interactive
  back_to_player: the walk card (only pointer-eating element) is geometrically clamped out of the top bar where the Learn escape lives, on every step, notch-aware — the player is always one tap away

offering_surfaces:  # invitations, not missions — NOTHING auto-plays, ever
  noticing_invitations: rules.json CTA target 'walk:<id>' renders as a button (NoticingInvitations.vue) that starts the walk in place
  how_this_works: HowThisWorks.vue card lists matching node-home walks as Show-me links
  walk_offer_mounts: NodeInsightsView (node-insights), ClassDetail (class-detail, teacher only), AdminInvites (admin-invites)

genre_reuse:  # 2026-08-06
  rule: >
    The card genre may be reused by a surface that is NOT an engine walk, via
    WalkCard.vue — but such a surface must never call startWalk, never appear
    in the pack, and never claim to be a walk in the engine's sense. The
    engine's own invariants (never auto-play, never trap, anchored to real
    elements) are unchanged and remain compile-gated.
  first_consumer: >
    components/admin/ManagerOnboardingGate.vue — the org manager's password
    step (a GATE: fires unbidden, blocks, no skip) and the PWA install nudge
    (a PROMPT: always escapable). The password step could not be an engine
    walk without breaking compile gate 7 (never-auto-play), so it borrows the
    genre only. See apml/schools/node-home.apml manager_onboarding_gate.
  gap_closed: >  # founder ruling 2026-08-06, superseding the open_gap flagged above
    CLOSED. The durable anchor now exists: components/admin/YourAccount.vue —
    a permanent "Your account" card on the member node home, where a leader
    sets or changes their password and installs the app AT ANY TIME, not only
    at first login. Its three anchors (account-card · account-password ·
    account-install) sit on ROW containers rather than buttons, so they exist
    in every state — including "already installed", where there is no button
    to point at — and the two pack walks below can never find nothing.
    ManagerOnboardingGate is UNCHANGED: it stays the front door for a
    brand-new manager, and this is the second, permanent home for the same two
    actions afterwards.

real_data_ruling: >
  Walks run on the real page over real data. Show-and-point by default; click
  steps only on safe/reversible verbs (compiler-enforced denylist); admins
  rehearse write-heavy flows inside demo orgs.

walks_v1 (11):
  - invite-first-teacher: node-home (school) — admin/leader/school_admin
  - run-class-session: class-detail — teacher
  - invite-first-person: node-home (org) — admin/leader — the NEUTRAL-dressing twin of invite-first-teacher: same anchors, group-leader/learner vocabulary (founder gap 2026-08-03, orgs at schools parity)
  - ways-in: node-home (org/group/school) — admin/leader/school_admin (the re-mint-kills-old-link trap; the ledger is dressing-neutral, so the org kind is offered it too)
  - reading-insights: node-insights — admin/leader/school_admin
  - invites-desk: admin-invites — admin (show-and-point only)
  - share-a-class: class-detail — teacher — adding a co-teacher: who can be added, and that they get the whole class but not the lead (A-74, 2026-08-06)
  - invite-a-supply-teacher: class-detail — teacher — the CLASS-scoped co-teacher link for a colleague with no account yet, held apart from the student join link
  - hand-over-the-lead: class-detail — teacher — passing the lead, and what does NOT move with it (pupils, progress, sessions, your own place on the class)
  - move-a-teacher-between-classes: class-detail — teacher — the class↔teacher relationship read the OTHER way round ("which classes does this person take?"), via Other classes → the tick list. Teaches that a move is one untick plus one tick, and that belonging to several classes is just several ticks — the two things Tom went looking for on 2026-08-08 and could not find (2026-08-08)
  - set-your-password: node-home (org/group/school) — leader — anchored to YourAccount.vue; the link you came in on will not last, and this is the way back (founder ruling 2026-08-06)
  - install-the-app: node-home (org/group/school) — leader — anchored to YourAccount.vue; context-aware by device (installPlatform), and NOT one-time — the row waits however long the leader takes to change their mind
